1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,000
We're The Big Four, for the
Lunar Landing Site Navigator challenge.

2
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:08,000
At the Moon's south pole, the Sun skims the horizon.
Landers need sunlight for power and Earth in view to call home.

3
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:11,000
This is CLPS Lunar Mission Browser.

4
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:18,000
Pick a landing date and compare sites: sunlight, Earth time,
longest night and a verdict, from NASA JPL data.

5
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:22,000
See when the Sun and Earth next rise or set after landing.

6
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:26,000
Add any spot on the Moon of your own.

7
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:29,500
Students can press "Explain it to me".
Clearer landing choices, for everyone.
